#|
Advanced, explicitly enabled direction-sensitive mapping.

Input suffixes choose a branch: x+ right, x- left, y+ down, y- up,
v+ wheel up, v- wheel down, h+ wheel right, h- wheel left.
Each branch contributes a POSITIVE magnitude; its gain sets output direction.

- Pointer up moves right instead; pointer down still moves down.
- Wheel up moves right by 30 pointer units per notch.
- Wheel down still scrolls down. Horizontal scrolling stays native.
- Normal horizontal pointer motion works in both directions.

Unlisted OUTPUT rows keep identity in both directions. Within an explicitly
listed row, unlisted input branches contribute nothing.
The default mode is linear; this mode must be explicitly requested.
|#

(defcfg
  process-unmapped-keys no
  mouse-axis-map-mode directional
  mouse-axis-map (
    (x (x+ 1) (x- -1) (y- 1) (v+ 0.25))
    (y (y+ 1))
    (v (v- -1))
  )
)
(defsrc)
(deflayer base)
